(Description)
You are given an n x n 2D matrix representing an image, rotate the image by 90 degrees (clockwise).

- You have to rotate the image in-place, which means you have to modify the input 2D matrix directly. 
- DO NOT allocate another 2D matrix and do the rotation.

--- Solution ---
class Solution {
    public void rotate(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n / 2; i++) {
            for (int j = i; j < n - 1 - i; j++) {
                int temp = matrix[i][j];

                matrix[i][j] = matrix[n-1-j][i];
                matrix[n-1-j][i] = matrix[n-1-i][n-1-j];
                matrix[n-1-i][n-1-j] = matrix[j][n-1-i];
                matrix[j][n-1-i] = temp;
            }
        }
    }
}

--- Approach ---
In rotating process, it approachs as a pattern.

[In the 3x3 matrix]
1. If a value is at the position [0][0], it should be [0][2] after rotation.
2. If a value is at the position [0][1], it should be [1][1].
3. [0][2] should be [2][0].

=> So the pattern of position is [i][j] should be [j][length - 1 - i].

Using the nested loop, it maps the starting point with i row & j col.
Then, it covers from the outer of matrix first, and get in deeper to serch its inner.

